    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2 tests passing, 0 failures).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` endpoint now rejects an owner whose normalized telephone already belongs to another owner, responding **409 Conflict**.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions:\n\n1. **`CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique`** (new function step) \u2014 reads the just-built `Owner` via `@Val`, compares its normalized (digit-stripped) telephone against every existing owner from `OwnerRepository.findAll()`, and throws a checked `DuplicateTelephoneException` on a match. It skips a record with the same id, so a re-save of the same owner isn't a false conflict.\n\n2. **`DuplicateTelephoneException`** \u2014 checked exception (`extends Exception`) so it surfaces in the `throws` clause.\n\n3. **`DuplicateTelephoneExceptionHandler`** + **escalation YAML** (`org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DuplicateTelephoneException.yml`) \u2014 turns the exception into a 409 `ProblemDetail`, matching the pattern used by the existing `InvalidTelephoneException` handler.\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `checkTelephone` step between `build` and `save` (`build \u2192 checkTelephone \u2192 save \u2192 respond`), so the check runs after the telephone is normalized but before persistence, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\nPlacing the check after `BuildOwner` means it operates on the normalized value, and normalizing existing owners' telephones on read keeps the comparison robust regardless of stored format.",
